    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for pet owners. The request may now include an ISO `birthDate`, and the owner's `ageBand` (`MINOR` under 18, `ADULT` 18\u201364, `SENIOR` 65+) is derived from it relative to `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges made, following the existing Spring/OpenAPI/MapStruct conventions in this repo:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `birthDate` input field to `OwnerFields` (optional, ISO date) and a read-only derived `ageBand` field to `Owner`. DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`birth_date` column) field with getter/setter, so it survives to read time when `ageBand` is computed.\n\n3. **`mapper/AgeBandResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the band as whole years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` (`<18` \u2192 MINOR, `18\u201364` \u2192 ADULT, `\u226565` \u2192 SENIOR), returning `null` when no birth date was supplied. This mirrors the existing `MembershipLevelResolver`/`LocalityResolver` pattern, kept out of the mapper so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired an `ageBand` mapping expression that calls the resolver. `birthDate` maps implicitly (present on both DTO and entity).\n\n5. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table across all supported databases.\n\nThe test suite passes: `coreDerivesAgeBand` creates an owner with `birthDate` `1990-01-01`, and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `ageBand: \"ADULT\"` (age 36 as of the default registration date). `BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
